==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|hlæja}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*hlahjaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈl̥aiːja/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|aiːja|s=2}}
*: {{homophones|is|hlægja}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|hló|hlógu|hlegið}}

# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[laugh]]
#: {{ux|is|Að '''hlæja''' dátt.|To '''laugh''' heartily.}}

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s6|hl|æ|j=j|mp=-|pp=-}}

====Derived terms====
{{der-top}}
* {{l|is|hlæja að}}
* {{l|is|hlæja hátt}} (to laugh [[loud]])
* {{l|is|hlæja hugur við}} (to gladden one's heart)
* {{l|is|skellihlæja}}
*:: The tidings, that '''gladdened''' their '''hearts'''.
*: ''Þau tíðindi, er þeim '''hló hugur við'''.''
{{der-bottom}}

